{"title":"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>How many of the following numbers are even?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe81f0a3fae75e2ae029fc07a57a489afdd81ba3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16\\text{, }29\\text{, }450\\text{, }34\\text{, }11\\text{, }N\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 1\">player 1</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c996acd51c78d9ece0ff3d8e78057e9a77fbbb6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. This makes the list:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d30323d56c301ba11dfc2c18699a09ea9775b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16\\text{, }29\\text{, }450\\text{, }34\\text{, }11\\text{, }5\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>From this, we see that the even numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/4739126bff84658daf38a400b94af84c72f11fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$450$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/3/433d742232f7bf3512c11eb996630ff5ead3641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" /> numbers here.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC\">2021 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 1\">Practice Relay Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEM